{
  "uid": "azure-aks-prometheus",
  "title": "Azure / AKS / Cluster (Prometheus)",
  "description": "AKS landing page from Azure Monitor managed service for Prometheus (default minimal-ingestion metrics only; no recording rules required). Drill down with the links to the built-in 'Managed Prometheus' dashboards (from Azure/prometheus-collector) that Azure Managed Grafana installs when an Azure Monitor workspace is linked; they are not managed here. Managed by Terraform (azure-managed-grafana): edit dashboards/aks/aks-cluster-prometheus.json.tftpl, not the dashboard in the UI. Changes made in Grafana are overwritten on the next apply.",
  "tags": [
    "azure",
    "aks",
    "kubernetes",
    "terraform"
  ],
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "schemaVersion": 41,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "1m",
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "Kubernetes / Compute Resources / Cluster",
      "type": "link",
      "url": "/d/fd0cac08a3f34e2994cf904627836738?var-datasource=$ds&var-cluster=$cluster",
      "icon": "dashboard",
      "keepTime": true,
      "includeVars": false,
